Software Requirements Specification (SRS) 
Project: Max Potential 
Version: 1.0
Date: 09.07.2026

1. We are Max Potential Software, founded in 2016. We are a software company that specializes in designing and integrating systems for businesses that need organization in order for them to succeed.  We acquired this project by referral from one of our previous clients in the parking garage industry. They saw our work at another location and wanted to integrate a similar system into their business. 

1.1 The purpose of this project is to be able to develop a plan that can successfully be able to integrate a system that can use the space to place parking spaces efficiently. Alongside this, the project will also include features that make it easier for customers to navigate, such as lights that direct drivers where to go, park, and exit. Customers will be able to see which parking spots are available and which are being used, with also be able to pay online to reserve a specific spot, add time to their reservation, or cancel their reservation at any time. Overall, the goal is to have customers be able to navigate the parking garage more efficiently, without hassle or confusion. More features such as electric vehicle parking stations would be installed, some smart lighting for light costs to go down, and the installation of solar panels to power lights, gates, and pay stations. 

1.2 The scope of this project is to successfully integrate a system for both customers and workers to be able to more efficiently navigate the parking garage. What is out of scope is doing major structural upgrades, which would take too long to complete and are out of the client's budget. 

2. Overall Description 
  Users: Customers of the shopping center, people who work near the parking garage, gas vehicle users, electric vehicle users, and employees who oversee the business. 

System Environment: Mobile app, Website, and Kiosks 

Constraints: Must run on secure hardware for payment processing and authentication

Assumptions: Application has internet service and a secure connection.

3. Functional Requirements 
FR1: System will allow customers to sign up or log in in 2 steps
FR2: System allows users to see and add inventory to the cart for purchase
FR3: System will allow employees to sign in
FR4: System will keep a record of sales and the number of customers
FR5: System will automatically send reports to administration
FR6: System will work in collaboration with physical kiosks for payment 
FR7: System will automatically reboot with backup power in result of a loss of power

4. Non-Functional Requirements
NFR1: System will update inventory in real time
NFR2: System will have to support at least 2500 users simultaneously 
NFR3: System must have an uptime of 99.99%

5. Use Case Examples 

Title: Reserving a parking spot
  1. Customer selects parking spot number
  2. Parking spot is added to cart
  3. Customer is sent to checkout page 
  4. Customer completes purchase.

Title: Customer signs up for email updates
  1. Customer signs in
  2. Customer clicks "account"
  3. Customer clicks "email preferences" 
  4. Customer agrees to receive email updates 

Title: Customer Resets Password
  1. Customer clicks "forgot password"
  2. Customer fills out email 
  3. Customer inserts old and new password
  4. Customer confirms new password

Title: Customer inserts new payment method
  1. Customer signs in
  2. Customer clicks "account"
  3. Customer clicks "add new payment method"
  4. Customer fills out new payment details
  5. Customer clicks "save" 

Title: Customer deletes old payment method
  1. Customer signs in
  2. Customer clicks "account"
  3. Customer clicks "remove payment method"
  4. Customer clicks save

Title: Adding time to reservation from app
  1. Customer signs in
  2. Customer clicks "Reservations"
  3. Customer clicks on their current reservation
  4. Customer clicks "add time"
  5. Customer is taken to checkout page
  6. Customer completes purchase

Title: Customer is checking out via Kiosk
  1. Customer walks up already with ticket in hand
  2. Customer inserts ticket
  3. Kiosk displays purchase amount with time, location, and date
  4. Customer presents payment method
  5. Customer completes purchase 

Title: Customer wants to see available spaces for reservation
  1. Customer signs in
  2. Customer clicks "start reservation"
  3. Customer is presented with all parking spots available in green and unavailable in red on a map

Title: Employee wants to check reports for the month
  1. Employee signs in with their company ID and password
  2. Employee clicks "reports"
  3. Employee is brought to reports page
  4. Employee clicks "filter"
  5. Employee clicks on "Monthly" 
  6. Reports for that month are filtered for the employee to overlook
